------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Origin and derivation
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Grandpa is a derivative work of OpenJarvis, an Apache-2.0 licensed project
developed by The OpenJarvis Authors and contributors. OpenJarvis is itself
derived in part from IPW (Intelligence-per-Watt).

This repository retains the full commit history of the upstream project.
Commits from 2026-03-12 through 2026-05-22 are the work of the OpenJarvis
contributors. Grandpa was established on 2026-05-23, and commits from that
date onward are the work of The Grandpa Authors.

Grandpa has been substantially modified from its upstream origin. It is a
Windows-first local AI assistant; OpenJarvis was a general agent and
inference platform. Substantial portions of the upstream platform layer
have been retained, extended, or removed. Files whose module docstring
records a direct derivation from IPW are, at the time of writing:

    src/grandpa/core/registry.py        "Adapted from IPW's src/ipw/core/registry.py"
    src/grandpa/engine/_stubs.py        "Adapted from IPW's InferenceClient"
    src/grandpa/agents/_stubs.py        "Adapted from IPW's BaseAgent"
    src/grandpa/agents/prompt_registry.py  "Adapted from IPW's prompt_registry.py"
    src/grandpa/core/events.py          "Extends IPW's EventRecorder"

This list is not exhaustive as to derivation; it records the files that
carry an explicit upstream attribution in their own docstring.

Both the upstream work and this derivative are licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. See the LICENSE file for the full license text.

